        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0086" n="1046" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1046"/>

                <head>No. 717.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stallo to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1888-08-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 21, 1888</date>. (Received
                        September 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 230.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A telegraphic dispatch from Mr. Jones, our
                    consul at Messina, which I have just received, informs me that the
                    procurator-general of the court of appeals, in Messina, has moved the court to
                    discharge Salvatore Paladini, and not to permit him to be extradited, on the <pb
                        facs="0087" n="1047" xml:id="pg1047"/> ground that he is an Italian subject.
                    I have requested Mr. Dougherty to communicate to the Department whatever
                    official notice of this result may be given to the legation after my
                    departure.</p>
                <p>In this connection I take the liberty of requesting the Department to send me the
                    latest edition of the “Treaties and Conventions concluded between the United
                    States of America and other powers.” The copy I find in the legation library is
                    very imperfect and consists, in part, of loose sheets.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Stallo.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
